<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11701" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crŭcĭārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		crux, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to the cross</i>, or, in
			gen., <i>to torture.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exitus,</span>”
				<i>full of torture</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Praescr. Haeret. 2</span></i>
			 dub. (al. cruciatorios): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poenae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst., one who is crucified</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Petr. 112</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Contr. 3, 21</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> As a term of reproach, <i>one fit for the gallows, a gallows-bird</i>,
					<i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 242</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">longum est quae cruciarius ille conflavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 2, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
